42
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:16,135
a variable I could price.

43
00:03:16,536 --> 00:03:22,997
Mira Reiss-Marsh was born on the second of February
2089 at the most scientifically capable

44
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:29,051
location on the planet, attended by a midwife from
Raccoon City who had been flown in

45
00:03:29,071 --> 00:03:33,966
for the purpose and who was the most
frightened person in Antarctica.

46
00:03:34,366 --> 00:03:40,174
She was, by every measure, an ordinary infant. She
cried, she fed badly for four days,

47
00:03:40,194 --> 00:03:41,936
she had her mother's chin.

48
00:03:42,336 --> 00:03:47,979
She has, at the end of this account, no detectable
upper limit to her lifespan, an immune

49
00:03:47,999 --> 00:03:53,452
system that has never been challenged by anything,
and a cellular repair rate that her

50
00:03:53,472 --> 00:03:59,053
grandmother's generation would have called a miracle
and that she considers unremarkable

51
00:03:59,073 --> 00:04:01,725
because everyone she grew up with has one.

52
00:04:02,126 --> 00:04:04,555
She is two years old when the sky opens.

53
00:04:04,955 --> 00:04:10,886
The narrator mentions her here, in a quiet chapter,
because she is the reason the last

54
00:04:10,906 --> 00:04:16,976
twenty-nine chapters of this story are not a tragedy,
and because she is the only person

55
00:04:16,996 --> 00:04:22,165
